{"id": "EUVD-2026-67552", "enisaUuid": "985127b4-21da-334a-af7f-3dbd66a8667d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nDrivers: hv: vmbus: use generic driver_override infrastructure\n\nWhen a driver is probed through __driver_attach(), the bus' match()\ncallback is called without the device lock held, thus accessing the\ndriver_override field without a lock, which can cause a UAF.\n\nFix this by using the driver-core driver_override infrastructure taking\ncare of proper locking internally.\n\nNote that calling match() from __driver_attach() without the device lock\nheld is intentional. [1]", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:49:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1656234a4a2dc6e975546867887c5f63e4a90f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1cb12ae81d2f7a58b0b1cfb51862afca98e6058", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e2f0833556c8c5269deb457b89d538644a3b747", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fb010ea7ca98cd09a6d365260b769f627e73a76", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/331d8900121a1d74ecd45cd2db742ddcb5a0a565"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80676", "GHSA-pvqm-w959-q2j3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2b22b561-0bd6-380f-8e9e-30fe922d5efc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d765edbb301c0e196015a59b17420558088ea33f <2fb010ea7ca98cd09a6d365260b769f627e73a76"}, {"id": "3eb5baae-52f6-3ae9-8009-2ae508d07ac5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d765edbb301c0e196015a59b17420558088ea33f <0e2f0833556c8c5269deb457b89d538644a3b747"}, {"id": "57d85077-2c56-37c0-a99d-437734483ac8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d765edbb301c0e196015a59b17420558088ea33f <a1656234a4a2dc6e975546867887c5f63e4a90f0"}, {"id": "6fe4ea59-ef2c-3497-ae27-27cd2653bba6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_ver